 "summary": "Mispaired: paper Lemma 8.7 is about choosing five bump profiles so that an axisymmetric increment (∆v, γd) uniquely solves the integral constraints (8.25). The Lean theorem is an unrelated torus-averaging identity. It says that the square-average over z of the angular mean of a(z)·cos²(jθ+phase(z)) equals (|det(vr,vt)|/2)·(∫χ²)·actualColumn_i, where a is a periodized native slot field composed with an n-fold covering map. Most components (periodize, nativeField, slotChart, transverseStretch, pulseProfile, squareAverage, covering, period) are not visible, so even the Lean statement's own meaning cannot be fully checked.",
 "glossary": [
  {"decl": "actualColumn", "line": 12, "plain": "Vector with i-th entry ci·∫_ℝ ψ(v)²·x(v)·t(v)_i dv.", "standard_concept": null, "matches_standard": "unclear", "note": "Bespoke. The integrand is integrable here because ψ is compactly supported and ψ, x, t are continuous, so the junk value 0 does not arise."},
