  {"ref": "Lemma 8.7", "plain": "Assume the slow base satisfies (8.24) with λ > 0 and |a(η)| ≥ a0 > 0. Then there are three azimuthal and two axial bump profiles such that, for arbitrary targets (P, Jθ, Jz), a unique linear combination (∆v, γd) satisfies the five integral constraints (8.25). The resulting increments are linear in the targets, lie in the stated classes, and preserve the integral constraints."}
